{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788192940,"nonce":"TNRhQVOpvmzehRdAOxHexukQjj0=","title":"Prisoner capture and the prison room — its own research task, after the rest is done","message":"Evan, 2026-08-31, filed deliberately as LATER: \"capturing prisoners and having a\nprison room should be filed too, only after everything's done since taking care\nof / recruiting prisoners is its own research task.\"\n\nSo this is scoped as a placeholder with the reasoning captured, not a spec ready\nto dispatch. Do not pick it up ahead of the post-raid procedure (cc8988c).\n\nWHY IT MATTERS TO THE POST-RAID PROCEDURE\n\ncc8988c's finish-off step kills downed raiders. That is the right default ONLY\nbecause there is nowhere to put a prisoner. The moment a prison exists, the\ndeterministic branch flips: \"strip and capture\" replaces \"finish off\", and the\nprocedure gains treat-the-prisoner steps.\n\nThat flip is exactly the framework Evan is after — **a fact about the world\n(is there a prison?) deterministically changes which procedure runs**, with no\nagent judgement involved. It is worth building because it generalises, not\nbecause prisoners are important.\n\nWHAT MAKES THIS ITS OWN TASK RATHER THAN A STEP\n\nRecruiting is not one action, it is a standing programme: resistance and will\nhave to be worn down over many days, the warden interaction mode drives it,\nprisoner needs and health have to be maintained meanwhile, and the whole thing\ninteracts with mood, ideology and food. 3.4's `warden` verb already covers the\ninteraction-mode surface; what does not exist is the reasoning that decides who\nis worth recruiting and manages the campaign.\n\nWHAT ALREADY EXISTS, so this is not started from nothing\n\n- `warden {pawns, mode, enable/disable, recruitable, convert_to}` — shipped in\n  3.4, with the exclusive/non-exclusive split honoured and `Release` as a mode.\n- `dev:guest-status` for staging a prisoner on the bench.\n- `arrest` and `capture` — shipped in 3.4's order set.\n- The prisoner half of `pawns {filter:\"prisoner\"}` and PawnSafe's classifier.\n\nWHAT IS MISSING\n\n- Anything that builds or recognises a prison room. 3.3 (build verbs +\n  place-layout) is the dependency and is itself blocked on 1.9.\n- Prisoner bed assignment.\n- The recruitment campaign logic — whose home is the playbook, not C#.\n\nDeps: 3.3 (rooms/beds), cc8988c (the procedure this flips), and realistically\n4.2's play loop for the campaign half.","files":null}]}